.TH BREATHGSLB-LICENSEGEN 8 "September 2026" "BreathGSLB" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
breathgslb-licensegen \- mint BreathGSLB license keys and payloads
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B breathgslb-licensegen
.RB [ \-email\ \fIaddr\fR ]
.RB [ \-os\ \fIname\fR ]
.RB [ \-supportExpiry\ \fIYYYY-MM-DD\fR ]
.RB [ \-customerType\ \fItype\fR ]
.RB [ \-supported ]
.RB [ \-type\ \fItrial|standard|supported\fR ]
.RB [ \-config\ \fIfile\fR ]
.RB [ \-send ]
.RB [ \-smtp\ \fIhost:port\fR ]
.RB [ \-from\ \fIaddr\fR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B breathgslb-licensegen
mints a new license: a random 32-character key plus a JSON payload
carrying the operating system, licensee email, salt, support expiry,
support flag and customer type. The payload is sealed with AES-GCM
under the key and printed base64-encoded alongside it:
.PP
.nf
.RS
key: <32-char key>
payload: <base64 nonce+ciphertext>
.RE
.fi
.PP
Give the key to the licensee at runtime; supply the payload to the
server via its license-payload channel. Missing values are prompted
for interactively on stdin (email, support contract, expiry), so the
tool works both scripted (all flags) and attended (bare invocation).
.SH PRESETS
The
.B \-type
preset sets the support posture before prompting:
.TP
.B trial , standard
Support contract off.
.TP
.B supported
Support contract on; defaults the expiry to one year from today when
.B \-supportExpiry
is empty.
.PP
A JSON config file given with
.B \-config
prefills the operating system default.
.SH EMAIL
With
.B \-send ,
the key is mailed to
.B \-email
via unauthenticated SMTP to
.B \-smtp
(default
.BR localhost:25 ),
which requires
.B \-from .
The payload itself is never emailed, only the key.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-email " addr
Licensee email. Required (flag or prompt).
.TP
.BI "\-os " name
Target operating system, matched case-insensitively
.RB ( linux ,
darwin, windows); empty falls back to the runtime OS.
.TP
.BI "\-supportExpiry " YYYY-MM-DD
Support expiry date. Required when the contract is active.
.TP
.BI "\-customerType " type
Free-form customer type recorded in the payload.
.TP
.B \-supported
Mark the support contract active (may be set by preset or prompt).
.TP
.BI "\-type " preset
One of
.BR trial ,
.BR standard ,
.B supported .
.TP
.BI "\-config " file
JSON config file prefilling defaults.
.TP
.B \-send
Email the key after minting.
.TP
.BI "\-smtp " host:port
SMTP server for
.BR \-send .
.TP
.BI "\-from " addr
Envelope sender for
.BR \-send .
Required with it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success. Missing required values and mail failures exit non-zero
with the reason on stderr.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR breathgslb (8),
.BR breathgslb-licensectl (8),
.BR breathgslb.conf (5)
